# Commit and Push Automatically

When a task changes code or config and the relevant tests pass, commit and push before replying. Do not wait for the user to ask.

- Stage only the files the task changed. Leave unrelated edits and scratch files uncommitted (`.tmp/`, `__pycache__/`, `$null`, workspace and profile files).
- Match the existing message style: one sentence ending in a period, saying what changed and why.
- Push the current branch to `origin`.
- Do not commit when tests fail, when the change is incomplete, or when the user asked only for analysis. Say why in the reply.
- Committing and pushing is not deploying. Deployment and tunnel rules still apply.
